lens:
Mobile UX, accessibility and web performance, round 4. Tested as a 360x640 Android shopper in the Instagram in-app browser, plus 360x600, 360x560, 320x568, 390x664, 390x844, 412x732, 412x846 and a height sweep from 640 to 900 at widths 360, 393 and 412. Stress cases: bottom safe-area insets of 24, 34 and 48 px; Android fallback faces (Roboto and Noto Serif through a private fontconfig) with the brand fonts blocked; Android 'Font size' at 115% and 130% (emulated by scaling every computed font size, which is what WebView textZoom does); and WCAG 1.4.12 text spacing.

G3 holds. fold.png, added.png, fold-ad.png, screens_*.jpg and measure.json (04:30) are newer than prototype.html (04:28:28), and my renders match them: facts end at 562, the bar starts at 575, and there are no console errors. All of my round-3 fixes landed and measure as intended.

Probes ran over http://127.0.0.1 against an untouched copy (md5 49edcb03…). Speed was measured with CDP throttling (150 ms RTT, 1.6 Mbps, 4x CPU) at DPR 2 and 3. The fixes were checked on a separate copy, /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/ux_r4/proto/variant.html, built by mkvariant.py; the prototype was not edited.

Evidence is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/ux_r4/out/:
- folds.json, var_folds.json and fold_*.png, var_fold_*.png;
- textscale_compare.jpg, tall_compare.jpg, focus_hidden.png;
- interact.json, interact_b.json, perf.json, perf_variant.json, vcheck.json;
- load_strip.jpg, states_sheet.jpg, compare_folds.jpg.
The scripts are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/ux_r4.

score_now is the weighted mean of C1, C2, C12, C13, C14, C15, C16 and C20 (the same set as rounds 2 and 3): 381.6/44 = 8.67.

criteria.note:
The card sits over the photo and never reaches the H1:
- 85–360 at 360x640 (85–364 after its + Add);
- compact 85–293 at 360x560;
- no suggestion, 85–225 at 320x568;
- 85–343 at 390x844 and 412x732 (85–372 after its + Add).
It has no timer and closes on ×, Escape, Keep browsing or 150 px of scroll. The bar reads '✓ Added to bag' for 600 ms, then 'Bag & checkout · ₹2,399', named '…, 1 piece'. The badge and the live region ('Prism Rivière Bracelet added. 1 piece in your bag, ₹2,399. A second piece takes 10% off your whole bag.') confirm the add. The card's + Add becomes an inert '✓ Added', and no card appears while the set is on screen.

All three round-3 faults are fixed. What remains is the dock covering spec rows and links (see C15).

fixes.change:
Make the first screen a column in which the photo gives way, never the facts.

1. Add this CSS:
.above { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: calc(100vh - var(--hdr) - var(--bar) - var(--safe) - 13px); height: calc(100svh - var(--hdr) - var(--bar) - var(--safe) - 13px); }
.above .gal { flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 180px; max-height: min(125vw, 520px); }
.above .track { height: 100%; }
.above .facts { flex: none; }
Delete both clamp() lines on .track (their work moves to .above).

2. Let the facts wrap instead of overflowing:
.price { flex-wrap: wrap; row-gap: 0; }
.lk, .lad .k, .ship { white-space: normal; }
.ship b { white-space: nowrap; }
.lad ul { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }

3. Use unitless line heights, which are identical at the default size:
.ship { line-height: 1.385; } .lk, .lad .k { line-height: 1.334; } .lad .v { line-height: 1.223; }

4. Bar: .buybar { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(128px, auto); }

5. Write each rung label as <span class="k"><span class="nw">2 pieces ·</span> <span class="nw">10% off</span></span>, so a wrap falls after the dot.

6. Keep the @media (max-width: 349px) rules.

In the live SPA, build the same structure in JewelDetail. Extend the first-screen budget test to run at font scales 1.15 and 1.3 and at 412x900, asserting that the delivery + COD line ends at or above the bar and that the document is no wider than the viewport.

Add: html { scroll-padding-top: calc(var(--hdr) + 8px); scroll-padding-bottom: calc(var(--bar) + var(--safe) + 8px); }
Then a focused control, a fragment jump (#set, #policy) or a scrollIntoView never lands under the sticky header or the fixed bar.
In the live app: html { scroll-padding-top: calc(var(--navbar-h) + 8px); } on every page, and on the PDP add scroll-padding-bottom equal to the sticky bar plus env(safe-area-inset-bottom). Then the hard-coded scrollMarginTop values can go.

fixes.why:
C14: WCAG 2.2 SC 2.4.11 Focus Not Obscured (Minimum), level AA. Tabbing from the top (31 stops), these are entirely hidden behind the bar when focused (focus_hidden.png, interact_b.json):
- the WhatsApp link;
- @naira.flore;
- the ring's '+ Add';
- 'Add all four · ₹3,987'.
The ring thumbnail and both Riya tiles are partly hidden. The same applies to TalkBack and switch users, whose focus the browser scrolls against the viewport. With the rule injected at runtime the count is 0, and nothing else moves.

fixes.change:
Let the ruler keep its 320 px width at 320 px screens:
.sl.size { padding: 0 0 34px; }
.ruler { width: 100%; max-width: 320px; }
The 0 and 24 cm labels already sit 10 px inside the viewBox. At 360 px and wider nothing changes, because the grid centres the 320 px ruler.
